== 1. User Concern Analysis ==

=== Concern 1: Universal Block Duplication (Drift Risk) ⚠️ HIGH ===

'''Finding:''' All 4 infobox templates share ~85% structural similarity:
* Identical YAML frontmatter pattern
* Same noinclude documentation structure
* Identical #set property blocks
* Same HTML infobox structure
* Same controlled vocabulary patterns
* Same validation approach (nested #if)

'''Risk Assessment:'''
* '''Severity:''' High
* '''Impact:''' Changes must propagate across 4 templates; inconsistency likely
* '''Current Mitigation:''' Sync comments exist but are manual

'''Evidence:'''
```mediawiki
<!-- TEMPLATE-SYNC-GROUP: infobox-templates -->
<!-- TEMPLATE-VERSION: 1.1.0 -->
<!-- LAST-SYNC: 2026-02-12 -->
<!-- SYNC-WITH: Infobox_Idea, Infobox_Implementation, Infobox_Project -->
```

'''Recommendation:'''
# Create `Module:InfoboxBase` Lua module with shared validation logic
# Templates call base module with configuration table
# Single source of truth for validation rules

'''Prototype:'''
```lua
-- Module:InfoboxBase
local p = {}

function p.validate_and_render(frame, config)
    local args = frame.args
    local errors = {}

    -- Validate required fields from config
    for _, field in ipairs(config.required) do
        if not args[field] or args[field]:match("^%s*$") then
            table.insert(errors, "Required: " .. field)
        end
    end

    -- Validate controlled vocabularies
    for field, values in pairs(config.vocabularies) do
        if args[field] and not values[args[field]] then
            table.insert(errors, "Invalid " .. field .. ": " .. args[field])
        end
    end

    if #errors > 0 then
        return p.render_errors(errors)
    end

    return p.render_infobox(args, config.template_type)
end

return p
```

