=== Concern 2: #set Running When Required Params Missing ⚠️ CRITICAL ===

'''Finding:''' Current pattern in all 4 legacy infoboxes:

```mediawiki
{{#if: {{{Title|}}} | 
  {{#if: {{{Definition|}}} | 
    {{#if: {{{Domain|}}} |
      {{#set: ... }}  <!-- Only here is #set guarded -->
    | {{Error|Missing Domain}} }}
  | {{Error|Missing Definition}} }}
| {{Error|Missing Title}} }}
```

'''Problem:''' The pattern APPEARS to guard #set, but:
# Error template displays message but doesn't halt execution
# Parser continues processing after error display
# #set may execute partially if some params exist

'''Evidence from Infobox_Concept:'''
```mediawiki
{{#if:{{{Title|}}}{{{Definition|}}}{{{Domain|}}}|  <!-- Concatenation, not AND -->
{{#set:
 |Has page type=Concept
 |Has title={{{Title|}}}  <!-- Sets empty if Title missing! -->
```

'''Validation Test:'''
```mediawiki
{{Infobox_Concept
| Title = Test
| Definition =   <!-- EMPTY -->
| Domain = CS
}}
```
'''Expected:''' Blocked with error  
'''Actual:''' #set executes with empty definition

'''Recommendation:'''
# Use Lua module for strict validation
# Return empty string (halt) on validation failure
# Never execute #set with potentially empty values

'''Prototype Fix:'''
```lua
-- In Module:InfoboxValidator
function p.validate_concept(frame)
    local args = frame.args

    -- Strict required check
    if not args.title or args.title == "" then
        return '<div class="error">BLOCKED: Title required</div>'
    end
    if not args.definition or args.definition == "" then
        return '<div class="error">BLOCKED: Definition required</div>'
    end
    if not args.domain or args.domain == "" then
        return '<div class="error">BLOCKED: Domain required</div>'
    end

    -- Only now generate #set
    local smw_props = {
        ["Has page type"] = "Concept",
        ["Has title"] = args.title,
        ["Has definition"] = args.definition,
        ["Has domain"] = args.domain
    }

    return generate_smw_set(smw_props) .. render_infobox(args)
end
```

