=== Concern 3: Required Fields Not Actually Enforced ⚠️ CRITICAL ===

'''Finding:''' TemplateData documents required fields, but:
# MediaWiki doesn't enforce TemplateData requirements
# Template code has weak validation
# Error display doesn't prevent execution

'''TemplateData Example (Infobox_Concept_Improved):'''
```json
"title": {
  "label": "Concept Title",
  "type": "string",
  "required": true  <-- Only visual indicator
}
```

'''Actual Enforcement:'''
* Visual Studio Code extension may warn
* MediaWiki itself ignores "required": true
* Template renders with empty values

'''Evidence:'''
```mediawiki
{{Infobox_Concept_Improved
| title = My Concept
| definition =    <!-- EMPTY but required -->
| domain = CS
| epistemic_status = Established
| confidence = 0.9
}}
```
'''Result:''' Template renders with blank definition field

'''Recommendation:'''
# Implement L2 validation in Lua modules
# Return error HTML that blocks rendering
# Use guard clause pattern - validate first, render only if valid

'''Prototype:'''
```lua
function p.validate_required(args, required_fields)
    local missing = {}
    for _, field in ipairs(required_fields) do
        local value = args[field]
        if not value or value:match("^%s*$") then
            table.insert(missing, field)
        end
    end

    if #missing > 0 then
        return false, "Missing required: " .. table.concat(missing, ", ")
    end
    return true, nil
end

-- Usage
local valid, error_msg = p.validate_required(args, {"title", "definition", "domain"})
if not valid then
    return '<div class="bitwiki-validation-error">' .. error_msg .. '</div>'
end
-- Continue with rendering...
```

