=== Concern 4: Relationship Fields Underspecified ⚠️ MEDIUM ===

'''Finding:''' Current relationship handling:

```mediawiki
| Related concepts = Page1, Page2, Page3
| Related concept types = part-of, depends-on, related-to
```

'''Problems:'''
# No pairing between concept and type (by position only)
# No validation that target pages exist
# No cardinality constraints
# No semantic relationship direction

'''Evidence from Infobox_Idea:'''
```mediawiki
| Depends on = Concept A, Concept B
| Depends on relation types = requires, assumes

| Supports = Idea X, Idea Y  
| Supports relation types = enables, validates
```

'''Issues:'''
* If lists have different lengths, relationship is ambiguous
* No way to specify "Concept A requires, Concept B assumes"
* SMW stores flat values, not structured relationships

'''Recommendation:'''
# Use structured format: `PageName[relationship_type]`
# Parse in Lua to validate and generate proper SMW
# Create subobjects for complex relationships

'''Prototype:'''
```lua
function p.parse_relationships(rel_string)
    local relationships = {}
    -- Format: "Page1[part-of], Page2[depends-on], Page3"
    for entry in rel_string:gmatch("([^,]+)") do
        entry = entry:gsub("^%s+", ""):gsub("%s+$", "")
        local page, rel_type = entry:match("^(.-)%s*%[(.-)%]$")
        if not page then
            page = entry
            rel_type = "related-to"  -- default
        end
        table.insert(relationships, {
            page = page,
            type = rel_type
        })
    end
    return relationships
end

-- Generate SMW
for _, rel in ipairs(relationships) do
    smw_output = smw_output .. string.format(
        "[[Has relationship to::%s]] [[Has relationship type::%s]]\n",
        rel.page, rel.type
    )
end
```

