=== Concern 5: Controlled Vocabularies Not Enforced ⚠️ HIGH ===

'''Finding:''' All templates document controlled vocabularies but don't enforce them:

| Template | Field | Documented Values | Enforced? |
|----------|-------|-------------------|-----------|
| All | Epistemic status | Hypothetical, Provisional, Established, Deprecated | ❌ No |
| All | Stability class | Volatile, Evolving, Stable, Canonical | ❌ No |
| Concept | Concept type | Theory, Model, Framework, Principle, Pattern | ❌ No |
| Idea | Concept type | Hypothesis, Framework, Model, Principle, Conjecture | ❌ No |
| Implementation | Interface | REST API, CLI, Library, GUI, Smart Contract | ❌ No |
| Project | Status | Planned, Active, Completed, Suspended, Cancelled | ❌ No |

'''Current Pattern (Weak):'''
```mediawiki
{{#switch: {{{Concept type|}}}
| Theory = {{#set: Has concept type = Theory }}
| Model = {{#set: Has concept type = Model }}
...
| #default = [[Category:Template Error]]{{Error|Invalid...}}
}}
```

'''Problem:''' #default only triggers on non-matching values, but:
* Empty values pass through silently
* Typos like "Framwork" create new SMW values
* No centralized vocabulary definition

'''Evidence:'''
* Infobox_Concept allows ANY value for Concept type
* SMW property "Has concept type" has no [[Allows value::...]] constraints

'''Recommendation:'''
# Centralize vocabularies in Module:ValidatorBase
# Strict validation with clear error messages
# Add SMW property constraints

'''Prototype:'''
```lua
-- Module:ValidatorBase
local VOCABULARIES = {
    epistemic_status = {
        ["Hypothetical"] = true,
        ["Provisional"] = true,
        ["Established"] = true,
        ["Deprecated"] = true
    },
    concept_type = {
        ["Theory"] = true,
        ["Model"] = true,
        ["Framework"] = true,
        ["Principle"] = true,
        ["Pattern"] = true
    }
}

function p.validate_vocab(value, vocab_name)
    local vocab = VOCABULARIES[vocab_name]
    if not vocab then
        return false, "Unknown vocabulary: " .. vocab_name
    end
    if not value or value == "" then
        return true, nil  -- empty is valid (optional field)
    end
    if vocab[value] then
        return true, nil
    end
    local valid = {}
    for k, _ in pairs(vocab) do table.insert(valid, k) end
    table.sort(valid)
    return false, "Invalid value '" .. value .. "'. Valid: " .. table.concat(valid, ", ")
end
```

